Z||000000||cmyokley||06-22-99||04:24 PM||||Help...I am about to blow MY head gasket.<br>My son and I have spent the last 18 months rebuilding his 86GT. We are about to finish the rebuild and are having a nagging problem with the motor. <p>We rebuilt the 2.8L with all new parts, .030 over pistons/new crank/new cam etc..all stock. We have also replaced the O2,IAC,TPS,MAT,engine temperature (one to ECM), water temperature, oil pressure sensors, along with the EGR Solinoid valve. About all I can think that I have not replaced is the MAP and the EGR tube.<p>The problem after all this is the engine still lacks power...like it is in OPEN LOOP.<p>I have (now) no codes on the ECM, I did have 22 and 32, but those cleared up.<p>The engine starts and idles well, although the idle is at 1200 to 1400 RPM, but when you push it in 2nd or 3rd gear it just isn't responding like it should.<p>I have done so much reasurch on the WEB, but my patience is running out.<p>Could I have a simple vacume leak, bad egr tube, bad ECM? Will a dianostic test reveal the Problem?<p>Compression is 150 to 155 PSI and fuel pressure is in spec.<p>The smell from the engine is like it has too much fuel...not burning all fuel...<p>I am trying to think about everything so maybe someone can HELP...<p>Thanks
Z||000001||lowCG||06-22-99||04:41 PM||||Kinda sounds like an ignition problem of some sort,can you watch the spark advance with a timing light? Is the ignition properly grounded? Is the little button inside of the dist cap(if it has one)in good shape/springy? It doesn't backfire through the intake does it?
Z||000002||GREENDANO||06-22-99||07:01 PM||||Make sure you grounded A to B in the ALDL connector before you set the timing.  I set mine with out grounding the terminal together and found out later that I had my timing retarded 12 degrees.  What a dog.  It's a beast now that I have the timing set right.<br> Dan-O
Z||000003||Cooter||06-22-99||07:50 PM||||I hope I dont insult you with this one, but did you get the distributer "in time" by putting no. 1 at TDC and making sure that matches up to the no. plug wire? Dont laugh, I've done it before and the engine ran like a dog. Check all engine to chassis grounds, and chassis to battery grounds. Another one that I hope doesnt insult- is the throttle opening up all the way? 
